{
  "description": "Spec 029: workspace.snapshot.v3 is workspace.snapshot.v2 plus an optional agent_integrations array, so the phone can say when a host is missing the integration that lets it see an agent. workspace.snapshot and workspace.snapshot.v2 never carry the field (their apps decode results strictly). A v3-aware app retries v2 only on method_unknown. The host omits the field until its first background probe lands, so a snapshot never waits on agent CLIs.",
  "fields": {
    "agent_integrations": "Optional, v3 results only. At most 8 entries, one per agent CLI the host detects; an agent that is not installed at all has no entry.",
    "agent": "Open vocabulary, [a-z_] and at most 32 bytes. Today: claude, codex, pi. An app ignores an entry whose agent it does not know.",
    "state": "Open vocabulary, [a-z_] and at most 32 bytes. Today: installed, missing, needs_approval (codex hooks not yet trusted in Codex), outdated (an update is available), unsupported_version (installed, but the agent runs a version this host refuses). An app ignores an entry whose state it does not know."
  },
